  "solution": "Here the pattern followed in **each column** is:\n\n**{(3rd number) – (1st number × 10)} ÷ 5 = 2ⁿd number **\n\n**Column 1:** 10, 12, 160\n\n{(3rd number) – (1st number × 10)} ÷ 5\n\n= {(160) - (10 × 10)} ÷ 5\n\n= (160 – 100) ÷ 5\n\n= 60 ÷ 5\n\n= 12 **= 2ⁿd number**\n\n**Column 2:** 13, 11, 185\n\n{(3rd number) – (1st number × 10)} ÷ 5\n\n= {(185) - (13 × 10)} ÷ 5\n\n= (185 – 130) ÷ 5\n\n= 55 ÷ 5\n\n= 11 **= 2ⁿd number**\n\nSimilarly,\n\n**Column 3: 17, ?, 235**\n\n**{(3rd number) – (1st number × 10)} ÷ 5**\n\n**= {(235) - (17 × 10)} ÷ 5**\n\n**= (235 – 170) ÷ 5**\n\n**= 65 ÷ 5**\n\n**= 13** **= 2ⁿd number**\n\nHence,** “13” **is correct answer",
